# Copy to .env and fill in. .env (and every .env.* variant) is gitignored —
# BACKEND_MIMO_API_KEY is a live billable credential and this repo is public.
#
# Seven variables, and exactly one of them is uncommented, because exactly one
# has to be supplied. The rest are commented out and show the value the binary
# already uses.
#
# Everything else about how mimostats probes — the model pair, the price table,
# the system prompt, the retention window, the whole timeout ladder — is a
# constant in backend/internal/config/config.go, not a setting. Those describe
# what the dashboard measures rather than where it runs, and a deployment that
# could change them could publish a differently-shaped number under the same
# page. Each one carries its rationale in a doc comment next to the value.

# --- The only required setting ---
# The tp- token-plan key. The container refuses to start without it, by design:
# a keyless deployment would record an unbroken wall of auth failures, and the
# dashboard would render that as a MiMo outage.
BACKEND_MIMO_API_KEY=tp-replace-me

# --- Server ---
# BACKEND_ADDR=:8080
# BACKEND_LOG_LEVEL=info
# The container mounts ./data at /data. Overridable because hack/dev.sh runs the
# daemon straight on the host, where /data does not exist and cannot be created.
# BACKEND_DB_PATH=/data/mimostats.db

# --- MiMo endpoint ---
# The token-plan host the tp- key is issued against. Both mimo-v2.5 and
# mimo-v2.5-pro are served here.
#
# This value must never carry a credential: no user:pass@ and no ?api_key=.
# The daemon refuses to start on either. The key goes in BACKEND_MIMO_API_KEY
# and nowhere else.
#
# The TCP ping target for MiMo's edge is DERIVED from this hostname and has no
# setting of its own — pinging one host while inferring against another would
# put a latency figure on the page for a path no request takes.
# BACKEND_MIMO_BASE_URL=https://token-plan-sgp.xiaomimimo.com/v1

# --- Europe->Singapore reference (bare hostname or IP; no scheme, no port) ---
# Answers "is *any* Europe->Singapore path healthy", so a MiMo-specific fault
# can be told apart from a broken route. OVH, because the probe box is on OVH
# and a same-carrier path makes "the route is fine" a stronger claim.
#
# The one probe target that stays configurable: proof.ovh.net is OVH's public
# per-datacentre speedtest node, which is marginally more renumber-prone than
# the rest of this file. Point it elsewhere if it stops answering, or if this is
# deployed somewhere the OVH backbone is not the relevant path.
#
# See DefaultRefSGPHost in backend/internal/config/config.go for the two OVH
# names that do NOT work, recorded so they are not re-tested.
# BACKEND_PING_REF_SGP_HOST=sgp.proof.ovh.net

# --- Probe user agent ---
# Impersonates opencode, because that is what MiMo's token-plan endpoint sees in
# production: probes present as a real coding agent on purpose, and a neutral
# client would not measure what production traffic experiences. Still settable,
# because what the endpoint sees from real clients is a fact about the outside
# world rather than a decision this repo makes — both compose files pass it
# through.
# BACKEND_PROBE_USER_AGENT=opencode/1.18.11 ai-sdk/openai-compatible/3.0.20 ai-sdk/provider-utils/5.0.18 runtime/bun/1.3.14
